From 31a6fc18afac39edcb89284b74c8e522b1d761dc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:24:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VIF1 + VU1 thread (opt-in, GA2_VU_THREAD=1): exact, but not
 faster in GA2

ga2_vuthread runs VIF1 and VU1 on their own thread, as PCSX2's MTVU: each
DMA pass's PATH3 and VIF1 data is copied (DMA still completes at once on
the game thread) and run there in order, ending with the arbiter's drain.
Sync points (the EE waits for the thread): VU1 memory (mapVuMemory), the
GIF/VIF registers and the VIF1/GIF FIFOs, GIF packets submitted from the
game thread, the native GIF fast paths, VIF1 downloads, the GS entries and
the paraLLEl-GS readback/vsync; the frame tick's scan-out marker goes
through the thread's queue (at most one tick waiting). On the thread the
MSCAL/MSCNT callbacks leave the EE context alone; passes with VU1 D/T stops
enabled stay on the game thread.
SIGNAL/FINISH/LABEL and the display registers keep their EE timing: the
game thread scans each pass (gifRaisesCsr, and vif1RaisesCsr, a mirror of
the VIF1 parser's command sizes with STCYCL tracked and checked against the
real state after every pass) and splits it at the DIRECT that carries
such a packet; the thread takes what comes before, the game thread waits
and runs the rest. A CSR bit raised on the thread (only possible from a
VU1 XGKICK packet) is reported. The governor's load is now the busiest of
the game thread, the VU thread and the GS worker (ga2_vuthread busy time;
native/compat/ga2_framerate.cpp).

Measured (RTX 4090, Zettai ship map, 1x, 175 cap, governor off): 159.8
frames/s with the thread, 167.7 without. Every frame's VIF1 chain in GA2
ends with a 2-qword DIRECT writing FINISH, whose interrupt (IMR 0xfd00:
enabled) the EE waits for 2000 cycles later, so with exact timing the VU
work stays on the critical path and the copies and hand-off only add
cost. Hence off by default; overlapping it would need a later FINISH
delivery, which changes what the game sees.

Proof (4x, GA2_FREERUN, research/run59/gpu-175/proof5): with the thread vs
without, the GIF capture is byte-identical over 106 MB, frame signatures
agree at all 15290 common game times, present shots identical, no scan
resync and no CSR bit raised on the thread; English dialogue as before;
ps2x_tests 641/641, gs_cache 45/45.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
